  "reading": "Down-dominance does NOT come from systematically harder criterion thresholds: only 104/464 boundary cells are harder vs 187 easier (173 equal), and star-delta cells are near-balanced (4151 down vs 3135 up; 3588 vs 3135 excluding the degenerate 2026 D07 MA-PD split). The asymmetry is produced at aggregation: (1) net weighted per-contract shocks skew negative among >=4.0-rated contract-years in EVERY year (2024: 244 neg / 69 pos; 2025: 159/86; 2026: 188/45), i.e. the down-moves concentrate on the high-rated contracts' measure profiles while up-moves concentrate in pools of lower-rated contracts; (2) the degenerate 2026 D07 MA-PD split (empty boundary list -> every contract 5->1) supplies a large uniform negative shock in 2026; (3) an UP flip must traverse from a median raw of ~0.27-0.31 below the 3.75 line, while DOWN flips harvest the tail of 4.0-rated contracts sitting just above it."
